WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.883 --> 00:00:13.053
Tune Your Brain is our library of short brain games. Anyone can play, and when you're signed in, your scores and badges are saved. This video shows you how to play, and how to track your progress.

2
00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:18.075
At the top, you'll see how many games you've played and how many badges you've earned.

3
00:00:18.576 --> 00:00:27.606
Under Choose a Game, use the filter buttons to narrow the list by grade band, or by the skill a game builds. Select All to see everything again.

4
00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:32.049
Each card tells you what the game works on. Select Play Now.

5
00:00:32.552 --> 00:00:38.122
Choose a difficulty, then select Start Game. Easy is a good place to begin.

6
00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:48.755
Flip two cards at a time to find the matching pairs. The counters at the top track your moves, your misses, and the time. When every pair is matched, the round ends.

7
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:06.760
Your score appears, with your moves, your accuracy, and your time. You also earn experience points, and sometimes a new badge.

8
00:01:07.261 --> 00:01:17.971
To see how you're doing, go back to the library. Your game cards now show your level and best score, and Your Progress appears at the top. Select View full dashboard.

9
00:01:18.472 --> 00:01:28.812
The dashboard shows your level and experience, your streak of days played, your totals, and a card for each game you've played. Your recent games are listed at the bottom.

10
00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:39.403
Badges are on their own page. Earned badges are in color, and the ones still to win are shown so you know what to aim for. You can also choose which badges to show off.
